  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(0.1)+2(0.4)+3(0.15)+4(0.2)+5(0.05)+6(0.1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.8+0.45+0.8+0.25+0.6 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
